{
  "name": "candidates are staged privately, then contacted irreversibly",
  "description": "ADR-0008 §3a and ADR-0023. Staging somebody on a job discloses NOTHING: no email, no notification, no row in contact_requests. A separate, deliberate contact step raises every request in one transaction and cannot be undone.\n\nThe rule it serves is that a contacted contributor can never be un-contacted — once somebody has been told a company is interested, that is a fact — and a rule that strict is only tolerable if there is a moment before it binds. That moment is what the mis-click remedy below is: Carol is staged, removed, and never learns either happened.\n\nTHERE IS NO SHORTLIST. A round was always one-to-one with a role (ADR-0019 §3), so it was a second name for the job carrying a second title and a second status that could disagree with the role's. The people hang off the role, and 'who have we approached for this' is one question with one answer.\n\nThree properties are pinned that a re-implementation loses first: the contact step is IDEMPOTENT (a second press with nobody new tells nobody and reports it), it is INCREMENTAL (somebody staged on day 3 is told and the others are not re-told), and the promised date is COPIED onto each request at the moment of sending, so nothing the company does afterwards rewrites what a contributor agreed to.\n\nREWRITTEN FOR ADR-0024. A role no longer has one `location`, an `address_id` and a list of `eligible_countries`: it holds a set of location entries — remote from anywhere, remote within a named country, or onsite at one of the organisation's addresses. The hirer reads every entry with `mode`, `country` and `address`; a contributor reads a country (or null for anywhere) and, for onsite, a city — never a street. The three old keys are gone from every request and response. The seeded role is one remote-anywhere entry, which is exactly what `location: remote` with no countries meant, so nothing else this case asserts moves.",
  "seed": ["principals", "catalogue", "repositories", "scored_population"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "_step": "AssertNotSelf fires at STAGE time, not when the emails go out. Discovering that a candidate is the recruiter's own account at send time is too late.",
      "as": "dave_hiring",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/org-roles/{{acme.id}}/roles/{{acme.role}}/candidates",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a004"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "cannot_shortlist_self"
        },
        "db": {
          "role_candidates": {
            "where": {
              "role_id": "{{acme.role}}"
            },
            "count": 0
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "An unverified hirer cannot put anybody on a job, even though staging discloses nothing.",
      "as": "pending_pat",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/org-roles/{{unverified_org.id}}/roles/{{unverified_org.role}}/candidates",
        "body": {
          "user_id": "01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000a001"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "error": "hiring_capability_required",
          "hirer_verified": false,
          "organization_verified": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "A hirer at ANOTHER org is refused at the organisation, before a role id is even resolved.",
      "as": "sam_studio",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/org-roles/{{acme.id}}/roles/{{acme.role}}/candidates"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 403,
        "_note": "403 not 404, and the difference is where the refusal happens: the org prefix is checked before any role is read, so Acme's role id is never looked up and nothing about it is confirmed or denied.",
        "body": {
          "error": "not_an_org_member"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/org-roles/{{acme.id}}/roles/{{acme.role}}/candidates",
        "body": {
